&lt;p&gt;Just a little something I wish I had when I first started working with AEM. Adobe Experience Manager can feel like a real chicken-and-egg situation—Adobe doesn’t provide an easy way to set up AEM instances for experimentation, so you’re kind of forced to learn on the job. That’s a tough spot to be in when a company is paying you to already know how to do AEM work.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>